/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    Each element of an outer table, reached through a second name made in the rabbit, is given a rabbit's series.

    A name records where the NAME was made; the store is judged against where what it reaches
    was made, which can be further out. Judged once everything is checked, so a later statement
    that lowers it counts too (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define keeper as a series of series of series of number.
Insert (a series of series of number) into keeper.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define alias as keeper.
    For each row in alias, repeat:
        Insert (a series of number with (1)) into row.
    Done.
Done.
State keeper.
